{
  "project": "StudioGhibliLauncher (Ghibli · Вітер над долиною)",
  "generated_note": "All 8 wallpapers were generated via gemini-3.1-flash-image and visually verified. Soot Sprite poses (soot-idle, soot-jump) were generated as a single style-locked 1x2 chroma-key #00FF00 sheet and extracted via color-difference chroma keying with green despill and shared body scale normalization. Calcifer and Kodama focus auras were generated via gemini-3.1-flash-image with luma alpha extraction. All 20 free-form 1990s Studio Ghibli cel-animation prop icons (19 TV apps + All Apps archive) were generated as 7 style-locked horizontal sheets via Gemini Web (Orca CLI) on palette-separated #FF00FF magenta and #00FF00 green chroma-key backdrops, extracted via analytical un-premultiplication + despill (preserving translucent glass highlights and interior cutouts), and visually verified on 3 backdrops and live Lenovo TV. The runner mini-game ('Політ крізь долину') uses hand-painted Kazuo Oga gouache seamless valley panorama and meadow ground (cosine wraparound crossfade, zero mirroring), 4x2 hand-drawn 1990s cel-animation hero sheets for 3 playable heroes (Soot Sprite on #00FF00, Kodama on #FF00FF, Totoro on #FF00FF) with true 4-frame alternating Contact/Passing run cycles, 2-frame animated crouch strips, shared scale & baseline foot alignment, and 4 hand-drawn cel obstacles (stump, Toro stone lantern, 2-frame flapping Spirited Away origami paper bird). All 3 background music tracks (Ogg Vorbis) and 19 UI/focus/confirm/runner SFX (PCM WAV) are cut and normalized from authentic Studio Ghibli OSTs (My Neighbor Totoro, Spirited Away, Howl's Moving Castle, Castle in the Sky, Princess Mononoke) and CC0 foley (Kodama rattle #478642, cast-iron hearth fire #243742), documented in docs/audio-provenance.json.",
